MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Hypnotic Eye feels like a natural next choice because You Should Be So Lucky made me interested in hearing more of Benmont Tench with Tom Petty and the Heartbreakers.",
    "The Breeze connects directly to my interest in Old Sock through Clapton's relaxed blues and roots sound; In My Soul also fits the soulful mood I enjoyed in Memphis."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Endless River shares a broad rock connection with my listening, but atmospheric instrumentals do not satisfy my current interest in bluesy songs.",
    "The Beatles expanded editions and the Bowie retrospective offer familiar material or broad collections when I would rather explore another album with a close connection to my recent listening."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The recommendations seem to assume that an interest in established rock musicians means I want releases from other famous rock acts regardless of their sound.",
    "They lean too heavily on familiar classics and extensive collections, even though my recent choices suggest interest in individual albums."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The specific musical connections from Benmont Tench to the Heartbreakers and from Old Sock to more Clapton matter more to me than a broad rock association.",
    "I rarely choose many records at once, so a promising country or roots connection can appeal without being strong enough to make me choose it today."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understood my interest in blues and roots music, but sometimes stretched that into a general appetite for famous rock acts and classic collections."
}
